{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility","id":958321,"title":"do the solar exalted suffer (a bit) from lack of versatility?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-26T11:57:45-07:00","id":958321,"title":"do the solar exalted suffer (a bit) from lack of versatility?","content":"ok, im still extremely new to the game. but we know that the solar exalted's main power are all things that average humans can do, just taking to their most extreme conclusion.<br /> <br /> thus i assume they are entirely incapable of,say altering,fate turning into animals, or shooting lasers from their eyes. <br /> <br /> speaking of which, of all the exalted(incliding any martial arts an sorcery circle) who are the most versatile?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T12:00:38-07:00","id":958326,"title":"","content":"Solars can still apply their culture hero logic to accomplishing a number of more overtly supernatural effects or processes, even if that logic conveys the mechanism as being something unlike casting spells.<br /> <br /> \u200bI would say that an argument of them lacking diversity would first need to establish what things like turning into animals can be applied to that Solars are fundamentally incapable of.<br /> <br /> \u200bLikewise, a question of who is most versatile should be clear on what the standards for versatility are.<br /> <br /> For instance, you can probably achieve a wider range of character concepts with Solars than with others, and an individual Solar can develop in or incorporate a number of different directions, but Lunars might include details in which a single Lunar can apply themselves effectively to multiple endeavours without deep investment in Charms or Abilities, including through the acquisition of extra shapes, so... which one is more versatile?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 08-26-2016, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T12:20:53-07:00","id":958337,"title":"","content":"right, let us ,for the purpose of this thread , define ultimate versatility as the ability to alter reality in nearly any way one desires.(on a small or big scale we're not talking power right now)<br /> and let's also subdivine it by&quot;altering reality fast(e.g thinking about it) or slowly(e.g some sorcerous ritual)<br /> <br /> so a dnd wizard is generally more versatile than a sorcerer.<br /> <br /> a vtm blood mage may be extremely versatile but needs time to physically cast the rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T12:28:43-07:00","id":958345,"title":"","content":"I remember an interesting discussion we had on this topic way back in First Edition. <br /> <br /> Solars were focused. A Solar focused on one ability set but they were largely unsurpassed in it. A Solar focused on Larceny would be the king of thieves, but his skills might not be all that useful in a fight or when etching a ring (unless perhaps it was a forgery). The Solar's Charmset was like a large, well-stocked toolbox - each Charm was a tool in the Solar's toolbox that could be used to solve problems. But if the Solar didn't pick up Charms in a given Ability, (he didn't have that &quot;tool&quot; in his toolbox) then he would likely be no better than a mortal in undertaking that endeavor. <br /> <br /> Lunars had versatility - they were capable of applying their Charms and powers to many different tasks. A Lunar focused on dexterity could apply his abilities to sneaking, to combat, to acrobatics, to crafting, and to all manner of tasks. Rather than being tools in a toolbox, a Lunar's Charms were supposed to be more like a Swiss army knife, capable of being used in several different ways to solve different problems. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile the Sidereal were somewhere in the middle - Sidereal Exalted tended to have focus like a Solar, but at the same time they would have attack problems form odd angles and had strange abilities which gave them some level of versatility in how they approached solving a problem, but at the same time it often meant they had to go about problem solving in counter-intuitive ways. They had a toolbox like Solars, but all of their tools were designed around the metric system and the nuts and bolts (problems) were all in the imperial system. Your tools were often just as good as a Solar's, but you couldn't use them on the problem in the straightforward manner. <br /> <br /> Of course, while the &quot;theory&quot; sounded cool, in practice this was often not implemented in a very successful manner and the different Charmsets have struggled to make this vision work. I am tentatively excited that the authors will be able to make this functional in 3rd edition. Supernals have given Solars a clear, core identity and hopefully that means the capabilities of other Exalted will be allowed to shine through. <br /> <br /> In general though, Solars are pretty damn versatile in their own right. They can do anything a human can do, only better - and when you stop to look around you at the things humans can do, well, Solars can do all of that and then some. A Solar might not be able to shoot beams from their eyes or set things on fire by touching them, but then a Solar can just shoot beams from their sword or set things on fire by, you know, setting them on fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T12:29:15-07:00","id":958347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958337#post958337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">right, let us ,for the purpose of this thread , define ultimate versatility as the ability to alter reality in nearly any way one desires.(on a small or big scale we're not talking power right now)<br /> and let's also subdivine it by&quot;altering reality fast(e.g thinking about it) or slowly(e.g some sorcerous ritual)<br /> <br /> so a dnd wizard is generally more versatile than a sorcerer.<br /> <br /> a vtm blood mage may be extremely versatile but needs time to physically cast the rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if we're talking slowly, an Exalted sorcerer is considerably more versatile than a D&amp;D wizard or a VtM thaumaturge. Sorcerous workings can do virtually anything, limited only by hard setting restrictions against true immortality, time travel and resurrection. Solar workings are something on a par with D&amp;D epic spells, and Solars, appropriately enough, are the best at using them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T12:32:45-07:00","id":958351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958337#post958337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">right, let us ,for the purpose of this thread , define ultimate versatility as the ability to alter reality in nearly any way one desires.(on a small or big scale we're not talking power right now)<br /> and let's also subdivine it by&quot;altering reality fast(e.g thinking about it) or slowly(e.g some sorcerous ritual)<br /> <br /> so a dnd wizard is generally more versatile than a sorcerer.<br /> <br /> a vtm blood mage may be extremely versatile but needs time to physically cast the rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div>For this sort of a question it would do well to remember that Exalted has roots (not exclusively, but especially) in Pulp Fantasy like Tanith Lee and Moorcock (sp?). Characters abilities express themselves less as reality-alterimg wish fulfillment, and more as base expressions of a subjects might. That is, the power of an individual flows not from their ability to change or alter reality like a D&amp;D mage or M:tA mage, but from an expression of what they are. While these may be overt supernatural abilities, these abilities are not external to the nature of the Exalted, especially in the case of the Solar.<br /> <br /> ...I hope that helps, on review it sounds like garbled pseudo-intellectualism","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":2711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","user":"Janissary87","date":".  Tanith Lee, god damn autocorrect! 08-26-2016, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T12:47:11-07:00","id":958356,"title":"","content":"You're thinking of Tanith Lee, Janissary87.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> In terms of what direct effects they can do, like, &quot;If you wrote this guy up as a superhero, what would you put on the 'superpowers' section of his biography?&quot; Solars are limited to stuff that's either superhuman or that follows from what Isator Levi called &quot;culture hero logic.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, like, a Solar can't shoot people with eye-lasers or telekinetic cutting blades. They can't extend their teeth on tentacles to bite people, or grow a snake from their palm like Scorpion in the first <i>Mortal Kombat</i> movie to extend and pull someone across the room to them.<br /> <br /> In terms of what they can <i>accomplish</i>, this is not, in effect, much of a limit. For example, while a Solar can't eye-laser someone to death, they can swing a sword so hard that it creates an ultrasonic killing wind shockwave to slice someone in half from the distance of a football field. There's not much you can really <i>do</i> with eye-lasers that you can't do with ultrasonic killing wind shockwaves. I mean, like, there's <i>some stuff</i> -- Superman can do complex brain surgery with his heat vision, and Solars can't -- but, again, a Solar can just do complex brain surgery by &quot;Being a superhumanly amazing neurosurgeon,&quot; especially when you take into account their ability to e.g. summon phantom glowing golden surgical equipment from nowhere as part of the whole sun-hero thing they can do.<br /> <br /> If you're thinking in terms of &quot;What sort of powers can I put on my character sheet and how can I make them stylistically different from the powers of guy sitting at the table next to me,&quot; especially in terms of superhero powers, yeah, Solars are limited.<br /> <br /> Now, ironically, if you define versatility as the ability to alter reality in nearly any way one desires, Solars are arguably <i>the best and most versatile</i> at that, because they're the best sorcerers and sorcery lets you do anything, as long as you're willing to do rituals and not just come up with effects instantly on the fly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T12:47:33-07:00","id":958357,"title":"","content":"Alchemicals are probably contenders for most versatile, as long as they have prep time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T12:52:21-07:00","id":958360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958357#post958357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alchemicals are probably contenders for most versatile, as long as they have prep time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not stylistically. In terms of having superpowers that appear to function according to a quantitatively different nature and set of rules from the next Alchemical, they're arguably even more limited than Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T12:52:21-07:00","id":958361,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say the Solars &quot;suffer&quot; from lacking the ability to do any of those things; they can do about anything they need to do! And esp. + Sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T12:54:45-07:00","id":958365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958357#post958357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alchemicals are probably contenders for most versatile, as long as they have prep time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Enter vaguely bat-like Soulsteel Alchemical","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T13:10:52-07:00","id":958376,"title":"","content":"Solars also tend to have the greatest ability to break outside they stylistic constraints of their exaltation as well. There's eclipse, occult and integrity charms that let you internalize spirit powers and do things like shoot eye lasers, if you try really hard. Also their really high essence charms tend to strain the boundaries as well, hiding bodily inside a persons shadow and puppeteering them, projecting your soul into somebody's dreams to fight their mental disorders, ect. <br /> <br /> And, of course, as people have said being the greatest practitioners of martial arts and sorcery means that firing a jet of flame from their fist or dissolving their opponents soul with music come easier to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 08-26-2016, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T13:20:27-07:00","id":958381,"title":"","content":"I will point out altering fate is pretty much something every exalt can do. Sids are ironically the worst at altering fate, but that's because the job of the Siderail exalted is to maintain fate. So if unless the current fate is deemed detrimental to Creation the Sids are more often expected to ensure things stay on script as opposed to altering. On the other hand Sids are also the ones who can look at Fate and so are less likely than a Solar to defy fate by saving someone's life when the person was probably fated to survive anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T13:26:10-07:00","id":958384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958356#post958356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're thinking of Tanith Lee, Janissary87.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, what I get for trying to type on a cell phone","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":2711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","user":"Janissary87","date":". 08-26-2016, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T13:27:10-07:00","id":958385,"title":"","content":"As someone playing a Lore Supernal Twilight, I can assure you that Solars are the most versatile by your definition.<br /> <br /> My character literally has the ability to create whole kingdoms and armies and magical automated war-golem factories and magical swords out of thin air by concentrating hard on it. And that's BEFORE you get to his ability to predict the future, summon the Ten Plagues of Egypt on a whim, or cause comets to smash his enemies unless they do what he wants just because. And tha'ts BEFORE you get to the fact that as a sorcerer, with a bit of time there's pretty much nothing he cannot do.<br /> <br /> Like...I can't bring the dead back to life and I can't go back in time. That's about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T13:29:45-07:00","id":958387,"title":"","content":"A Solar can't turn into an animal, but they can have all the skills they need to keep up with their Lunar Mate in the Wilderness. They can survive in the harshest climate. They can run with the pack. They can track down prey. They can kill with their bare hands. <br /> <br /> Lunars need to turn into an animal to do all that. Solars do that in their own body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T13:55:10-07:00","id":958397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958381#post958381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand Sids are also the ones who can look at Fate and so are less likely than a Solar to defy fate by saving someone's life when the person was probably fated to survive anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, as better at seeing Fate, they're also the best at knowing when &quot;Haha, I have defied Fate!&quot; isn't just &quot;Well, turns out you were actually fated to do that.&quot;, and better at knowing when &quot;I have defied destiny itself!&quot; isn't &quot;I just unintentionally caused the deaths of a bunch of innocent people 5 years later, and ruined my legacy to boot, through random butterflies!&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T15:55:45-07:00","id":958463,"title":"","content":"Kinda. They can't do any of those things, but they also don't need to. They can't shoot later beams but they don't need to because archery does it just as well. They can't alter fate but precise planning usually gets them there.<br /> They DO lack versatility in that an individual solar is usually really good at one thing and then mediocre to poor at everything else. Though most exalts save lunars have that problem.<br /> Or to put it another way, the primary limitations on the solars <i>charmset</i> are usually just thematic more than limits on actual application. The limitations on an individual solar on the other hand have to do with the fact that they don't have ten billion experience points to buy every charm with so they have to dedicate them self to one thing and then pick their battles. This is what makes circles so scary, they can do basically everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","user":"Lionmanguy","date":". 08-26-2016, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T16:28:54-07:00","id":958480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958360#post958360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not stylistically. In terms of having superpowers that appear to function according to a quantitatively different nature and set of rules from the next Alchemical, they're arguably even more limited than Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by that definition, the only Versatile Exalts are the Exigents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T17:27:17-07:00","id":958504,"title":"","content":"I have to wonder how much versatility is really relevant. I think that given the way the game is constructed, most people aren't going to have much trouble or lack of incentive to build towards the character concept that they want, and aren't really going to pursue actions that aren't covered by such.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat do you really <i>do</i> with versatility.<br /> <br /> \u200bEven talking about one possibility for how Lunar Charms are arranged... sure, you have to invest in fewer stats in pursuit of any given course, but you still have build in those directions. You will probably not typically get individual Charms that do lots of things.<br /> <br /> That's for the typical definition of versatility, mind. For the one presented by the original poster...<br /> <br /> Like the question of general versatility, I have to ask what &quot;warping reality&quot; really means; what do you do with it?<br /> <br /> A Solar with Medicine doesn't have versatility or reality warping, but they have a course and a structure that guides purpose and action, and I judge those things to be a lot better. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T21:42:17-07:00","id":958604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958387#post958387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Solar can't turn into an animal, but they can have all the skills they need to keep up with their Lunar Mate in the Wilderness. They can survive in the harshest climate. They can run with the pack. They can track down prey. They can kill with their bare hands.<br /> <br /> Lunars need to turn into an animal to do all that. Solars do that in their own body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming that the Solar has Charms in Athletics, Awareness, Brawl, Stealth, Survival, and scads of other Abilities. Most will typically have gaps somewhere, whereas Lunars can do that without any Charms at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T22:47:06-07:00","id":958614,"title":"","content":"You specifically mention shapechanging and manipulating fate. Those are specifically things that are the focus of other Exalted types. So let's do some comparison there.<br /> <br /> 1. Solars are culture heroes, exemplars of skill. If study or practice can make you better at a thing in this setting, then Solars, if they choose to study or practice that thing, can become <i>the best</i> at it. This extends to things such as sorcery and shaping the Wyld to your will, as well as Evocations.<br /> 2. Lunars embody maximum raw potential, have multiple natural forms, and can steal others. Their tricks are (in theory) more versatile, but (in theory) can't <i>quite</i> reach the heights a Solar can.<br /> 3. Sidereals' power is, in a way, similar to the Solars' but it is limited to weird, esoteric expressions that often can't be applied directly to the problem. The only things they have that Solars don't are astrology and easier access to Sidereal Martial Arts.<br /> 4. Abyssals are even more similar to Solars, but interpreted through themes of death. They're better at Necromancy and have patrons and probably better gear, but that's about it, in terms of things Abyssals have that Solars don't.<br /> 5. Dragon-Blooded have elemental-themed powers, institutional power, and lineage themes.<br /> <br /> Looking at these five, any one of them can be said to &quot;suffer&quot; by not having everything that the other four do, if you want to look at it that way... but if we're talking about versatility in terms of groups as a whole, I'd say that Solars are easily the most versatile. A Solar can be an expert in anything you like, while certain limitations and expectations are built into the other four types. In addition, if you want powers themed on the elements, blood, death, or whatever, just pick up an appropriate Artifact and start learning Evocations.<br /> <br /> Now, a Lunar or an Alchemical might be more versatile on an individual level, and that's useful, but most Solars are good at the things they want to be good at.<br /> <br /> It gets weird when you talk about Solars &quot;suffering&quot; in terms of versatility because they can't shoot laser beams from their eyes. I mean, a lot of people suffer from not being Superman, but it's not really something you precisely <i>miss</i> when you don't have it. Or so I assume, anyway. Eye beams are an extra capability someone has. Lack of eye beams isn't really a detriment to be counted as a negative in most conversations. What frame of reference are you using, for the base assumption to be eye beams?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T23:49:09-07:00","id":958622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958337#post958337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">right, let us ,for the purpose of this thread , define ultimate versatility as the ability to alter reality in nearly any way one desires.(on a small or big scale we're not talking power right now)<br /> and let's also subdivine it by&quot;altering reality fast(e.g thinking about it) or slowly(e.g some sorcerous ritual)</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay.<br /> <br /> In terms of altering reality, Sidreals would be most versatile when it comes to doing it 'fast' while Solars would be most versatile when it comes to doing it slow.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T01:12:24-07:00","id":958636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958622#post958622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay.<br /> <br /> In terms of altering reality, Sidreals would be most versatile when it comes to doing it 'fast' while Solars would be most versatile when it comes to doing it slow.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> right. sorcery is capped by your exaltation. but i also vaguely remember reading somewhere that sorcery doesn't get much stronger after the rank of essence you acquire it.<br /> <br /> so doesn't that mean that if a sidereal and a solar are extremely powerful individuals then solar sorcery may not be relevant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T01:36:33-07:00","id":958641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958636#post958636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so doesn't that mean that if a sidereal and a solar are extremely powerful individuals then solar sorcery may not be relevant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Adamant Circle Sorcery is <i>extremely</i> relevant. The Workings that can be accomplished at that tier are nothing short of amazing, and being Initiated into the Adamant Circle means that you can perform Adamant Workings more easily than someone Initiated into the Sapphire Circle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T01:41:09-07:00","id":958644,"title":"","content":"Versatility may be best expressed in terms of sorcery and artifact evocations, two systems that allow any splat to go out of theme and accomplish damn near whatever the player wishes. Solars excel at both, and have an entire game system shoehorned into one of their charm trees (wyld shaping) that allows them to recreate reality where the substance of the world is weak, which helps with the more onerous requirements of sorcerous workings and artifact manufacture (gathering materials and ingredients.) Solars have a strongly human theme, but that includes the human power to reshape one's environment and use technology (of a sort) to accomplish their goals.<br /> <br /> Versatility may be best expressed in terms of the forms one can wear. There was an excellent post in the context of an edition of days past, one that compared Solars and Lunars. Imagine every single one of them was individually tasked with infiltrating an identical fortification, to acquire some macguffin in secret without getting caught. Solar stealth and larceny specialists would be the best at this, and have the greatest success, but dang near every Lunar would have some shapeshifting form that would at least lend them the ability to <i>try</i>, even those who don't have a single dot in Stealth. Solars would have the best successes, but Lunars would have the highest success ratio. The same logic applies to combat, and their beefier forms, as well as any other primarily physical challenge.<br /> <br /> Versatility may be best expressed in terms of connections. It doesn't necessarily matter what you can do; what matters is what you can get done. The Sidereals and the Dragon-Blooded respectively, are unmatched in terms of heavenly and terrestrial resources. Though their own charms are limited, numbered, and bound by strange metaphor to exceedingly specific tasks, the Sidereals have access to astrology and all the favors they dare accept from the gods of heaven and earth. They don't necessarily have to do anything directly; they just have to discover who can, and what that person wants. That might seem quite a task, but they have direct access to the Loom of Fate itself. They can literally brute force search all of reality for the proper pawn, if necessary. The Dragon-Blooded do not have to try nearly so hard. They rule the mightiest civilization in the world and even the poorest among them (pitiful Nellens!) have armies, fleets, and cities at their disposal. For the vast majority of what they might want to accomplish, they do not <i>do</i>, they simply order it done. For what requires their direct intervention, they have dozens of family members, each a legendary hero in their own right, that might assist.<br /> <br /> Or maybe versatility is just a word embodied beings used to describe an advantage in a game that has no winners. What you can do, what you can be, who you know, these are all limited sets of <i>certainties</i>, which, quite frankly, sounds like a trap option to me. That there could be an obstacle to acting upon ones whims is foreign to the Fair Folk, who are their whims and have none. If you leave your pitiful identity behind, that which was you can very briefly experience a taste of formless infinity before becoming the Wyld, which is honestly the best any of you poor &quot;souls&quot; (ha!) can hope for.<br /> <br /> (And as for Deathknights? They don't particularly care what you <i>can</i> do, since what everyone <i>must</i> do is die. The rest is just details.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T02:13:40-07:00","id":958652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958636#post958636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> right. sorcery is capped by your exaltation. but i also vaguely remember reading somewhere that sorcery doesn't get much stronger after the rank of essence you acquire it.<br /> <br /> so doesn't that mean that if a sidereal and a solar are extremely powerful individuals then solar sorcery may not be relevant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Think of it more like this:<br /> <br /> Terrestrial Circle Sorcery is not especially more powerful for an Essence 5 character, than it was at Essence 1 when acquired. A couple numbers are higher, but overall you're still doing the same things, flinging a swath of obsidian blade-winged butterflies to annihilate everything in a direction, etc. <br /> <br /> Celestial Circle is appreciably more powerful than Terrestrial, and Solar Circle beyond that. If comparing a Solar Sorcerer of the Celestial Circle and a Lunar Sorcerer of the Celestial Circle, their Sorcery doesn't change that much from essence 3 to essence 5.<br /> <br /> But then the Solar initiates into Solar Circle Sorcery, and his capabilities explode. He picks up crazy spells like Total Annihilation and Benediction of Archgenesis, and phenomenally increases the scope of his magical power, well beyond what \\changed in his Celestial Sorcery spells going from Essence 3 to 5. He is leaps and bounds ahead of the Lunar, sorcerously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T02:55:51-07:00","id":958659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958652#post958652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think of it more like this:<br /> <br /> Terrestrial Circle Sorcery is not especially more powerful for an Essence 5 character, than it was at Essence 1 when acquired. A couple numbers are higher, but overall you're still doing the same things, flinging a swath of obsidian blade-winged butterflies to annihilate everything in a direction, etc.<br /> <br /> Celestial Circle is appreciably more powerful than Terrestrial, and Solar Circle beyond that. If comparing a Solar Sorcerer of the Celestial Circle and a Lunar Sorcerer of the Celestial Circle, their Sorcery doesn't change that much from essence 3 to essence 5.<br /> <br /> But then the Solar initiates into Solar Circle Sorcery, and his capabilities explode. He picks up crazy spells like Total Annihilation and Benediction of Archgenesis, and phenomenally increases the scope of his magical power, well beyond what \\changed in his Celestial Sorcery spells going from Essence 3 to 5. He is leaps and bounds ahead of the Lunar, sorcerously.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> but let's assume that the same solar and lunar continue until essence 8. is solar sorcery still relevant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T03:07:45-07:00","id":958661,"title":"","content":"Not that Essence 6+ is especially relevant in most scales, but I would say yes, because both the Solar and the Lunar SHOULD have their native charms' scopes limited in some way even as they ascend that high [even if 2e DotFA laughed at the idea of in any way limited Solars]. <br /> <br /> In general, culture heroes and whatever Lunars are don't simply think things and the world immediately changes to suit their desires, or whatever; they have to act, and their actions have to have some logical progression towards the consequence that is desired. Sorcery bypasses that to a degree; walking a circle around an area doesn't impart abundant fertility to the land, but Benediction of Archgenesis does just that, and the Solar can do that [as he has Solar Circle Sorcery] while the Lunar cannot. The Lunar may have some means within her Essence 6-8 charmset of doing something in the same conceptual direction, but it is most likely limited in some way, requires a greater investment of effort or sacrifice, etc.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the Solar finds Adamant Circle Workings far easier; he requires 2 fewer successes per roll, his rolls are an order of magnitude more frequent [base 1 week vs 3 months], it costs him less experience to cement the working. And they are pretty significant in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T03:46:12-07:00","id":958671,"title":"","content":"Sorcery is not about ultimate power, it's about being able to do a wide variety of things.<br /> <br /> \u200bA Solar will never rise to an Essence where their Charms could do everything that sorcery does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T04:19:55-07:00","id":958681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958659#post958659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but let's assume that the same solar and lunar continue until essence 8. is solar sorcery still relevant?</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you imagine a Lunar or Sidereal will be able to do at Essence 8 that will make Solar Sorcery irrelevant?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T04:26:12-07:00","id":958683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958681#post958681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do you imagine a Lunar or Sidereal will be able to do at Essence 8 that will make Solar Sorcery irrelevant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Learn broken SMA ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T07:38:52-07:00","id":958736,"title":"","content":"What, even, <i>is</i> &quot;altering reality?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T08:13:36-07:00","id":958743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958736#post958736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What, even, <i>is</i> &quot;altering reality?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>turning a chicken into an elephant that breathes fire is intelligent ,can speak and subsists on rocks.<br /> <br /> to give you a very extreme example.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> anyway so basically the solars are a bit like dnd warlocks.(who have an ability to create any magical item they wish even if their normal abilities are limited )<br /> <br /> so long as you have time to prepare the fact that you can't shoot lightning is irrelevant because you can make a hammer that does.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T08:23:50-07:00","id":958746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958743#post958743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">turning a chicken into an elephant that breathes fire is intelligent ,can speak and subsists on rocks.<br /> <br /> to give you a very extreme example.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not very extreme, and you don't need to warp reality to do it. Just use one of the workings that alters a living being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> anyway so basically the solars are a bit like dnd warlocks.(who have an ability to create any magical item they wish even if their normal abilities are limited ) </div> </div> </div>man what<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> so long as you have time to prepare the fact that you can't shoot lightning is irrelevant because you can make a hammer that does.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Or you could just use Blazing Solar Bolt. Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T10:02:39-07:00","id":958782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958743#post958743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">anyway so basically the solars are a bit like dnd warlocks.(who have an ability to create any magical item they wish even if their normal abilities are limited )</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you're going to get far comparing a single splat against a single D&amp;D class, even this question breaks down a bit on the individual Exalt level if I'm being honest. <br /> <br /> A dawn caste, supernal Melee, who for some reason eschews non combat abilities is not really versatile if you consider social situations, running a city or performing sorcery. But he can create a sword out of sunlight and his will in the time it takes him to think about it. He can shoot bolts of fire from his blade, bat away the eruption of a volcano with a hammer and generally find a way to defeat anything in combat. He cannot however change a chicken into a fire breathing elephant, conceal his desires, or run a business. <br /> <br /> A twilight who focuses on sorcery and occult and not combat isn't in a very good fighter, but he can summon minions to fight for him, he can obliterate cities in a day. He can change lifeforms and the metaphysics of creation.<br /> <br /> Top this off with access to martial arts and greater sorcerous heights than any other exalt can reach? As a whole the Solars absolutely have massive versatility and diversity. An individual Solar might be limited but even they can solve many problems just by bludgeoning through with the things they are good at. <br /> <br /> The short answer to your question is: No.<br /> <br /> Also, yes, Solar Circle really counts at any essence level, but I really feel like in third edition talking about essence levels above five for exalts is a bit pointless at this time as we have no example for what those might look like. That means it is defined each individual table, so your answer could vary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/944864-abyssals-in-death-s-dream-kingdom-homebrew-wip-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals</a><br /> <br /> My attempt at a homebrew for Abyssals, focusing on unique charms.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11602-five_gee","name":"Five_Gee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T10:20:13-07:00","id":958787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958736#post958736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What, even, <i>is</i> &quot;altering reality?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Playing a primary caster in D&amp;D 3.x. Making context, planning, and story irrelevant by your ability to cast &quot;lolnope&quot; (later <i>Lolnope, Greater, Lolnope, Mass,</i> and of course, <i>Lolnope, Mass Greater</i>).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T10:37:42-07:00","id":958793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958787#post958787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Playing a primary caster in D&amp;D 3.x. Making context, planning, and story irrelevant by your ability to cast &quot;lolnope&quot; (later <i>Lolnope, Greater, Lolnope, Mass,</i> and of course, <i>Lolnope, Mass Greater</i>).</div> </div> </div> </div>or a mage in mage the ascension<br /> <br /> perhaps i should have phrased it differently . of all the exalted which are the most obviously magical?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T10:45:50-07:00","id":958796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958793#post958793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or a mage in mage the ascension<br /> <br /> perhaps i should have phrased it differently . of all the exalted which are the most obviously magical?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, it really depends upon the individual. What is more obviously magical? Turning into an animal? Firing golden bolts of energy from your sword? Twisting fire into a weapon? Taking the sword arm from a skilled man to steal his talent? Calling upon the powers of death or fate?<br /> <br /> Those are all pretty overtly magical things. And any exalt can learn martial arts to purge people of their sins with righteous fire or turn into a dragon floating through the air and covered in eyes. Any exalt can also work to conceal their powers as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/944864-abyssals-in-death-s-dream-kingdom-homebrew-wip-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals</a><br /> <br /> My attempt at a homebrew for Abyssals, focusing on unique charms.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11602-five_gee","name":"Five_Gee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T10:47:02-07:00","id":958797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958743#post958743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">anyway so basically the solars are a bit like dnd warlocks.(who have an ability to create any magical item they wish even if their normal abilities are limited )<br /> <br /> so long as you have time to prepare the fact that you can't shoot lightning is irrelevant because you can make a hammer that does.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure why conceptualizing a character like this is a boon to the rpg or the way it's played.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":2711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","user":"Janissary87","date":". 08-27-2016, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T10:50:28-07:00","id":958801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958793#post958793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or a mage in mage the ascension<br /> <br /> perhaps i should have phrased it differently . of all the exalted which are the most obviously magical?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Solar, Infernal, and Abyssal Exalted, who are better at sorcery and sorcery-like things than any other type of exalt. Or any exalt who chooses to learn martial arts so they can turn into a gazelle-carp thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11456-nihnoz","name":"nihnoz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11456_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T11:41:34-07:00","id":958819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958793#post958793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or a mage in mage the ascension<br /> <br /> perhaps i should have phrased it differently . of all the exalted which are the most obviously magical?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you asking who has the potential to be the most magical, or who can least avoid being overtly superpower magical? Because while a solar can have, basically, no overt super magical powers at all, they can also be the greatest martial artists, sorcerers and occultists.<br /> <br /> The thing is, being a sorcerer isn't just about making magic workings, if you have Benediction of Archgensis as one of your control spells, then life springs up and flourishes in your wake, even against your will the ground you trod becomes green and verdant, and if you stay in a dark woodland cabin for a few days the woods become like the forest from The Last Unicorn.<br /> <br /> Then, of course, if you have Death of Obsidian Butterflies your shadow flickers about with butterfly shapes and your fingernails can grow long shards of volcanic glass. Or if you have the burning words merit you just whip chains of fire from your hands. <br /> <br /> So if it's who CAN be the most magical, Solars, who MUST be the most magical, Sids or DBs I think. It's not because Solars are less versitile though, it's because they're more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T11:47:44-07:00","id":958820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958743#post958743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">anyway so basically the solars are a bit like dnd warlocks.(who have an ability to create any magical item they wish even if their normal abilities are limited )<br /> <br /> so long as you have time to prepare the fact that you can't shoot lightning is irrelevant because you can make a hammer that does.</div> </div> </div> </div>A good comparison for Sorcery would be 3rd edition D&amp;D item creation. In 3rd edition, if you wanted to craft a magical item, you would have to spend experience points to make it. So if a player wanted to brew a few potions, scribe some spells, perhaps make a wand of dispelling and a staff of lightning, they would be spending experience points to make those. In exchange for the extra versatility those items bring that player might be a level or even two or three levels behind the other players. Are those magical toys worth a few levels? Some people thought yes, some people thought no.<br /> <br /> Sorcery (and Workings) in Exalted are a bit similar to that. Sorcery spells are often very specific tools that can solve a given problem in one single way. Let's say you're a Sorcerer and come across a locked door - you don't have the Larceny to pick the lock or the Athletics+Strength to bash down the door. So you learn The Violent Opening of Closed Portals spell - it's a spell that, when you knock on a door, immediately annihilates every door, window or other object that bars entrey into a given structure - doors are blasted off their hinges and windows are shattered. It works on every single entrence and egress to a building and is incredibly obvious.<br /> <br /> A useful spell if you don't care about everyone knowing you're there and if you have to open every single door of a building at once. On the other hand, if you were hoping to be a bit more sneaky, this spell is totally useless.<br /> <br /> So if you ever come across a door you need to open and alerting everyone in the vicinity that you are coming isn't a big deal, this spell can be very handy. On the other hand, whenever you're not faced with an obstacle this spell can solve it's basically just taking up room on your sheet - and that was 8 experience you could have spent learning a Charm instead. If you have to wipe out a city of the map, Rain of Doom is one of the coolest effects in the game. But when you're not wiping out cities? It doesn't do much.<br /> <br /> So while the Sorcery toolbox is very versatile (if you're faced with a problem there's a spell that can solve it) at the same time each Sorcery spell is incredible not-versatile and can often only be used to solve very specific problems and when you purchase those spells you're not spending experience points on Charms, which can often be used in more situations than the very specific Sorcery spells (though I admit there are a few exceptions here and there - God-King's Shrike is basically Rain of Doom).<br /> <br /> Workings are similar - you have to spend experience points to make a Working. This creates an opportunity-cost and a player who makes a lot of workings might find himself falling behind other players who are constantly spending their experience points on upgrading their characters. Players have to carefully decide what kind of working they want and have to judge the creation of it based against other choices the experience points could have been spent on in a way that's very similar to 3rd edition D&amp;D crafting.<br /> <br /> So basically Sorcery and Workings are the most versatile toolboxes, but each specific Charm or Working is typically not versatile and often has limitations on how you can use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 08-27-2016, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T11:55:37-07:00","id":958823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958793#post958793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">perhaps i should have phrased it differently . of all the exalted which are the most obviously magical?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the problem here is that you're asking the wrong questions and focusing on the wrong things.<br /> <br /> A Solar that knows Blazing Solar Bolt can fire a beam of pure energy from their sword, which they created out of golden power projected from them.<br /> <br /> A Solar Sorcerer can summon massive tentacles made of lava and fires a massive beam of destruction, before going off to spend some time making their kingdom into a literal flying kingdom through a Working.<br /> <br /> A Solar Craftsman can use Craftsman Need To Tools to walk up to a bench with various metal ingots, breathe on them and wave their hands mystically, and have the finest sword any mortal has ever seen that's not made of Jade <i>in just a few minutes</i><br /> <br /> A Solar focusing on the Occult skill can see and strike at immaterial spirits, force them to become material, draw a mandala to contain them, and dive into a possessed person to help them fight off the spirit possessing them.<br /> <br /> A Solar Martial Artist can vanish into shadow with Ebon Shadow Style, leap from cover and break an arm with their bare hand (Tiger Style), then turn to another guy and hit them on the forehead with a chakra point strike to blind them (Snake Style).<br /> <br /> A Solar Brawler can grapple a triceratops, stop its charge, then heft the thing, swing it around, and throw it across to the other banks of a particularly wide river.<br /> <br /> And that's just SOLARS. That's not getting into how Sidereals pluck at the strands of Fate, how Lunars can be any creature, or wear more or less any face, how the Dragonbloods command the forces of the elemental dragons, how the Abyssals walk among the dead and bring the forces of the Underworld to bear, how the Getimians twist and rend Destiny and reality around them to suit their needs...<br /> <br /> <b>EVERY</b> Exalt is obviously magical as <i>fuck</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T12:04:03-07:00","id":958827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958793#post958793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">perhaps i should have phrased it differently . of all the exalted which are the most obviously magical?</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars are probably the &quot;least&quot; obviously magical. While they certainly have obvious powers and can unleash their caste mark and anima power, many of their Charms tend to be a bit more subtle and not innately overt and can easily be confused for peak natural mortal skill.<br /> <br /> Liminals are probably the most obviously magical - many Charms seem to unnaturally warp and twist their bodies, make them bleed blood from their eyes and when their anima ignites their true nature as a cobbled together inhuman monster is revealed to everybody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T12:22:40-07:00","id":958832,"title":"","content":"More accurately, any Exalted can, if desired, be a blatantly magical being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T12:27:10-07:00","id":958833,"title":"","content":"Also, Exalted generally doesn't go in for instant free-form magic systems, so there isn't an Exalt type that can do the sort of blatant arbitrary reality-alteration under discussion here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T12:31:59-07:00","id":958836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958793#post958793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or a mage in mage the ascension<br /> <br /> perhaps i should have phrased it differently . of all the exalted which are the most obviously magical?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted takes a very different approach to magic than mage: the ascension, derived from eastern mysticism and pulp fantasy. The kind of magic that you're thinking of is represented most closely in Exalted as Sorcery, which is open to any of the Exalted. It's where you have spells and runes and mystic words and needing the stars to be aligned just right and special incense burning as hooded figures gather in a circle around a pentragam to chant. In that sense, none of the Exalt types are magical at all! They leap mountain ranges, run across water, take on the aspect of a raging giant through their semi-divine nature and being &quot;just that good&quot;. So consider Exalted as offering a different idea of what magic &quot;is&quot; and what it means to be magical than what you're familiar with. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/91-wandering","name":"Wandering","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar91_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T12:40:23-07:00","id":958842,"title":"","content":"right i believe i get it. solars are not <b>necessarily</b> magical.<br /> they can do with their subtle powers what others can(or even need) to do with flashier powers<br /> <br /> but if they want to be sorcerously flashy then with solar sorcery they are basically mage-gods.<br /> <br /> ok, thanks everyone for your responses!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T12:58:19-07:00","id":958854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958833#post958833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Exalted generally doesn't go in for instant free-form magic systems, so there isn't an Exalt type that can do the sort of blatant arbitrary reality-alteration under discussion here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean...Wyld-Shaping.<br /> <br /> I can will a whole nation into being out of seething formless chaos...and then, with but a thought, DESTROY that nation in order to make Voltron because giant robots are cooler than nation-states. It's not Mage, but Twilights who want to focus on reality control are pretty good at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T15:10:31-07:00","id":958907,"title":"","content":"That's a reductive take on those Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T18:54:54-07:00","id":959014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958659#post958659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> but let's assume that the same solar and lunar continue until essence 8. is solar sorcery still relevant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Workings can, among other things, sear a new fundamental law into the universe or change it in some other fashion. There is<i> never </i>a point in a Solar's career where that capability could become irrelevant. Yes, because it can take awhile to pull off, it's not the go to solution for everything, but, as a last resort, directly editing reality is a very, very, very useful (and scary) power to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T07:29:27-07:00","id":959234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958854#post958854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean...Wyld-Shaping.<br /> <br /> I can will a whole nation into being out of seething formless chaos...and then, with but a thought, DESTROY that nation in order to make Voltron because giant robots are cooler than nation-states. It's not Mage, but Twilights who want to focus on reality control are pretty good at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>By creating reality where there is none and creating or destroying what they already created. I think that the fact that it's all the Solar's will imposed on chaos specifically makes it somewhat worth remembering. And that anyone can, to some extent, get the Wyld to do stuff from them historically. SOlars just do it to a scale and to power no one else really can muster or come close to.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T09:32:16-07:00","id":959302,"title":"","content":"To put it shortly, I've never seen a Solar &quot;suffer&quot; from a lack of versatility. If it's outside his wheelhouse, he can oftentimes just wrestle it in; in fact, I suspect that's part of the myth-hero logic at play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T10:04:10-07:00","id":959315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958842#post958842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">right i believe i get it. solars are not <b>necessarily</b> magical.<br /> they can do with their subtle powers what others can(or even need) to do with flashier powers<br /> <br /> but if they want to be sorcerously flashy then with solar sorcery they are basically mage-gods.<br /> <br /> ok, thanks everyone for your responses!</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar charms aren't subtle. They're super-human, not extra-human. Extra-human here means more than human: laser vision, shapeshifting, elemental powers, and so on. Super-human means &quot;everything a human can do, but better.&quot; Sherlock Holmes has a superhuman mind, and Captain America has superhuman fighting abilities. Changing your personality like you change clothes, meditating and being completely invulnerable, becoming actual nothingness, becoming a bright-eyed-bright-haired engine of destruction is anything but subtle.<br /> <br /> Also, no, they're not &quot;mage-gods&quot; for two reasons. One, gods in Exalted range from very weak spirits to the nigh-almighty Incarnae. And two, sorcerers don't just shoot spells out; they have to gather energy from the environment, mold it, and release it. From Terrestrial to Solar, that's how it always works. So there are clearly more than a few differences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11538,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","user":"kingcrackers","date":". 08-28-2016, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T11:12:05-07:00","id":959340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/958321-do-the-solar-exalted-suffer-a-bit-from-lack-of-versatility?p=958743#post958743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the fact that you can't shoot lightning</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSure you can; use Fiery Solar Chakram.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}